From 7aabe773bebb2e0fcbb3acb6597e05136ccc7147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:21:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Overhead blending: the edge between two terrains wanders, and
 two variants of one terrain fade into each other

A tileset can give t.blend_mask_2 and up next to t.blend_mask; the client
picks one mask per edge from the edge's position, the same on both sides,
so a long edge between two terrains no longer runs as a straight band.
With t.blend_mask_same, two different variants of one terrain's blending
layer fade into each other across their shared edge and corner, so the
texture does not stop dead at the tile edge. Those pieces are cut to the
quarter tile next to the neighbour and made the first time they are drawn.
Tilesets without the new tags draw as before.
---
 client/tilespec.c | 280 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 252 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/client/tilespec.c b/client/tilespec.c
index 2447be4..2c14579 100644
--- a/client/tilespec.c
+++ b/client/tilespec.c
@@ -164,6 +164,10 @@ enum spec_file_types {
   SFILE_LAST
 };
 
+/* Overhead blending: t.blend_mask and up to this many minus one more
+ * (t.blend_mask_2 ...), one picked per edge so a long edge wanders. */
+#define MAX_BLEND_MASKS 8
